  "overview": {
    "title": "Taste of the Tafilalet",
    "p1": "Dates are the agricultural pride of the Ziz and the wider Tafilalet. In Erfoud they sit piled on market stalls — soft, semi-dry or firm depending on variety and season.",
    "p2": "Buying a small box is one of the simplest local gestures of a stop in town. Sellers expect a short chat and a clear price.",
    "p3": "Harvest peaks in autumn; good dates remain available year-round from storage."
  },
